{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration (config_005: scvi_n200, multi-profile, avgpool) achieves 0.650 accuracy, while the only multimodal test (config_030: scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) scored 0.632—slightly *worse* than RNA alone. Image-only models are very weak (0.21–0.23), suggesting the image signal is noisy. However, one data point with concat fusion is insufficient to conclude that multimodal fusion is inherently unhelpful; concat may simply overweight the weak image features. Question: config_031 changes only the fusion method from concat to weighted (keeping scvi_n200, resnet50, multi-profile, avgpool identical to config_030), directly testing whether a learned/rebalanced fusion can recover or exceed the RNA-only baseline. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable extension of the most recent multimodal result, resolving the critical design question of whether the image modality adds any value under a more flexible fusion. If weighted fusion still fails to beat 0.650, we gain strong evidence to abandon multimodal paths and focus remaining budget on RNA-only optimization (e.g., testing transformer aggregation with scvi_n200). If it does help, it identifies fusion as a key lever and justifies further multimodal exploration. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice given the current uncertainty."
}

